    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0298" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg278"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 8, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to my letter of the 28th
                    ultimo, I have the honor to state to you that her Majesty’s government do not
                    see any sufficient grounds for coming to the conclusion, upon the statements
                    contained in your letter of the 27th ultimo, that the steamer Georgia is about
                    to be again used for belligerent purposes. With a view, however, to prevent the
                    recurrence of any question such as that which has arisen in the case of the
                    Georgia, her Majesty’s government have given directions that in future no
                    ship-of-war, of either belligerent, shall be allowed to be brought into any of
                    her Majesty’s ports for the purpose of being dismantled or sold.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
